                <pb facs="0599" n="589" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg589"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/6–2948: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-06-29T17:00:00-04:00">June 29, 1948—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>950. Emb authorized reach agreement Chinese on basis recommended urtel 1178 June
                    29. Dept believes would be desirable obtain written assurances re substance 3
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>), 3 (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) and 3
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) but will leave it your discretion what
                    assurances along these lines, written or oral, should be requested. Should be
                    made clear to Chinese that any written assurances agreed upon will be made
                    public.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
